title: github sessions pass raw owner/repo keys to Session.turn — history restores under sanitized key, losing context across restarts
updated_at: "2026-11-02T06:19:38Z"
---
Found during B830 session-eviction work (Lane A report 2026-10-02): github passes raw owner/repo keys into Session.turn in some paths, so turn persistence writes DB rows under the raw key while the in-memory session table and load_restorable_history use the sanitized key (slash->underscore). Those github sessions lose history restore across daemon restarts today (and across eviction reloads). Pre-existing duality; eviction neither fixes nor worsens it (eviction relies on the same lazy reload every other connector uses correctly). Root-cause mirror of B822 (which fixed the model-override APIs); fix belongs in session_turn.ml/github.ml key normalization at the turn boundary. Repro: github webhook comment on a PR -> restart daemon -> session context gone despite DB rows under the raw key. Lane A's test suite used the sanitized key form; a regression test for raw-key turns should accompany the fix.

Decision (2026-11-02 batch): session lane after B816/B818 to avoid test_session overlap. Verified turn boundary propagates raw keys while session loading sanitizes. Canonicalize at buffered/streaming/try-turn boundaries consistently and add raw owner/repo persistence/reload regression coverage, considering already persisted legacy raw-key history.

Decision (source design review2026-11-02): canonicalize before turn closures (run_session_turn/try_turn) and align GitHub notifier registration plus resume/drain bypasses. Legacy raw-key history recovery must be unambiguous and only fill an absent canonical history; canonical history takes precedence, preserve conflicting originals and avoid blind merges across slash/underscore collisions. Source-grounded design receipt supplied to session implementer; regressions will cover buffered/streaming/nonblocking turns and restart/eviction restore.

Independent review2026-11-02 found and reproduced two blockers in candidate db1d8535 before merge: P1 legacy promotion assumes all rows are FTS-indexed, so enabling search after stored history can make Session.create abort with CORRUPT; P2 persisted background-task completions can bypass legacy holds and retain raw notifier/response identity. Both accepted for scoped fix with deterministic production-path regressions, atomic recovery and preserved held branches. Original worker resumed; candidate remains unmerged until independent rereview. All builds/tests/formatter wrappers now x-p35 only per explicit user direction.

Completed: db1d8535 plus fix1a8e0253 merged after fresh independent review and scoped PASS. Buffered/streaming/nonblocking turns, notifiers, persisted completion callbacks and legacy GitHub history now use canonical identity; unambiguous legacy data promotes transactionally, conflicting branches remain held. Partial/late-enabled FTS and held background completions covered by regressions. Lane quick7784 plus minimal/optimized/format passed remotely; coordinator exact combined master gate passed7831 tests in64.395s and make fmt-check on x-p35 (gate-B831-merged.log). No real database was modified for validation; production deployment not performed.